---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ServiceLinks from '../components/ServiceLinks.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { dots } from '../lib/patterns.js';
const ask = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Custom software for my business')}`;
const bodyBg = dots();
---
<Base title="Custom software for any business" description="Software and phone apps built around how your business already works: one login for your staff and customers, your records in a place you own, and the tools you already use connected.">
  <Hero variant="graph" seed={23} tall mapLabel="My portfolio" mapTo="/work" eyebrow="Custom software · Any business" title="Stop bending your business to fit someone else's software.">
    <p class="lede"><em>"We pay for five tools and still run the business on a spreadsheet."</em> Off-the-shelf software makes you work its way. I learn how your business runs and build around it, with your leaders' input at every step: the customer portal, the scheduling, the billing, and the reports, behind one login. You own the code and the data.</p>
    <a slot="actions" class="btn btn-secondary " href={ask}>Ask about your software</a>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section band-parallax">
    <div class="band-bg" set:html={bodyBg} aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Software built around how you work, with logins for your staff and, if you want, your customers.</li>
        <li>Your records kept in a place you own, backed up, and easy to take with you.</li>
        <li>Connections to the tools you keep: payments, email, calendars, and accounting.</li>
        <li>A phone app for your staff or customers, when the work happens away from a desk.</li>
        <li>Working software every week, a written guide at the end, and optional monthly care.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Good fit if</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You run the business on spreadsheets, email, and subscriptions that do not talk to each other.</li>
        <li>You pay per seat for features you never use and still lack the one you need.</li>
        <li>You have outgrown the off-the-shelf tool you started with.</li>
        <li>Your people work in the field and need the system on their phones.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="phone-apps">Phone apps</h2>
      <p>Some work happens in a truck, on a job site, or at a client's door. I build phone apps that connect to the rest of your system, so your crew can check a job, approve a request, or send a photo without a laptop.</p>
      <p>My main product is <strong>Field Agent</strong>, a phone app that talks to an AI assistant at your office. ChatGPT on your phone starts from zero: it has never seen your quotes, invoices, or customer email. Field Agent's assistant runs on your own computer, where those records live, and a <a href="/knowledge-assistants">knowledge assistant</a> keeps them indexed. Ask from the job site what you agreed with a customer, and the answer cites the quote. Ask for a follow-up, and it is drafted from the thread. Its Mission Control screen shows what needs you today. Your records stay on your machine, the phone reaches them over an encrypted line, and nothing changes until you tap Allow. {site.booking && <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-book>Book a demo</button>} <a href="/work#field-agent">See it on the Work page</a></p>
      <p>Another is <strong>Kingdom Guide</strong>, an iPhone app that plans a theme park day: the route, the waits, and the return times for families who use disability access, with every phone on the trip in step. <a href="/work#kingdom-guide">See it on the Work page</a>.</p>
      <h2>Where it comes from</h2>
      <p>Ten years building finance and healthcare platforms, where lost data or downtime costs real money. I led the move of one live platform's services to the cloud.</p>
      <p><span class="tag">Fixed scope</span> <span class="tag">You own the code</span> <span class="tag">Optional monthly care</span> <span class="tag">Quote on scope</span></p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={ask}>Ask about your software</a></p>
      <p class="muted">Need only a website? I build those too. <a href="https://flourishfinancialgroup.org">Flourish Financial Group</a> went live a month after the first conversation and costs $0 a month to host.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ServiceLinks current="/software" />
</Base>
